{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css font weight css font weight","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","fileName":"CSS Font Weight.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Font Weight","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CSS Web Typography]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Web Typography","CSS Font Matching","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css font weight css font weight","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","fileName":"CSS Font Weight.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Font Weight","heading":"CSS Font Weight","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The `font-weight` property selects how light or bold a font face should appear. CSS accepts named values such as normal and bold, numeric weights from 100 through 900, and relative values that seek a bolder or lighter face than the inherited weight.\n\nAvailable fonts may not supply every requested weight, so [[CSS Font Matching]] maps the request to a suitable face. An `@font-face` weight descriptor declares which requests a downloadable resource represents.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Web Typography","CSS Font Matching","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css font weight css font weight","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Weight.md","fileName":"CSS Font Weight.md","folder":"6 - Full